@@ -0,0 +1,237 @@
+# Prototype Score Normalization — Change Report
+
+Implementation of `prototype_score_normalization_and_class_aggregation.md`:
+per-prototype z-score normalization with appearance-weighted class aggregation.
+
+**Date:** 2026-07-26
+**Scope:** 5 files modified, 4 files added. No adapter `run()` loop was touched —
+both target settings are reached by config alone.
+
+---
+
+## Design decisions taken before implementing
+
+Three points where the spec did not map cleanly onto this codebase:
+
+| Question | Decision | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Where do `mu` / `sigma` come from? The doc says "training/reference split". | **Online running statistics** over the test stream. | This repo has no train split at all — every dataset class passes only `test=` to `DatasetBase`, and `utils/data.py` exposes only `build_test_data_loader`. Building one would have broken the TTA claim. Each image is scored using statistics from *previously seen* images only, then folded in, which satisfies doc requirement #9 with zero leakage. |
+| Prototypes that win no patch group score exactly `0.0`. Include them? | **Include** in both statistics and z-scoring. | A prototype that usually fires but is absent now yields a negative z — an active "this class's signature is missing" vote. Consequence: class scores can go negative, unlike the old `[0,1]` range. |
+| Z-scores are unbounded (~`[-3,+10]`) but `tau_patch_proto=20` was tuned for `[0,1]`. | **Sweep tau, and expose an optional `tanh` squash.** | Scale-invariant for `patch_only` (pure argmax), but the linear fusion in `patch_modulated_pta` genuinely needs rescaling. |
+
+---
+
+## Files added
+
+### `utils/proto_stats.py` — new, 183 lines
+
+Running reference-score statistics per prototype. Pure helpers, kept out of
+`utils/kmeans.py` so that file stays focused on clustering/scoring.
+
+State is three parallel `[K]` tensors held per class alongside `appearance`:
+`score_count`, `score_sum`, `score_sqsum`.
+
+| Function | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `init_stats(K, device)` | Three zero tensors. |
+| `has_stats(state)` | Guard for banks predating this feature. |
+| `accumulate(state, best_per_proto)` | Fold one image's raw scores in. Returns new tensors. |
+| `compute_mu_sigma(state, min_count, sigma_eps)` | `(mu, sigma, valid)`. Population variance via `E[x²]-mu²` with `clamp(min=0)` against catastrophic cancellation, then Bessel-corrected where `count > 1`. |
+| `zscore(raw, mu, sigma, valid, sigma_eps)` | `(raw-mu)/max(sigma,eps)`; invalid prototypes abstain at `0.0`. |
+| `grow(state, new_K, device)` | Pad accumulators when the bank grows; new prototypes start at zero. |
+| `permute(stats, keep_idx)` | Reindex to follow a prune. |
+| `low_variance_count(sigma, valid, sigma_warn)` | Doc requirement 1.4 — flag near-degenerate reference distributions. |
+
+`sigma_eps` defaults to `1e-6`, matching the existing `clamp(min=1e-6)` idiom at
+`utils/kmeans.py:229`.
+
+### `scripts/slurm_proto_zscore.sh` — new, 182 lines
+
+9 experiments × 7 datasets (`caltech101 dtd eurosat fgvc oxford_flowers
+oxford_pets ucf101`) → `#SBATCH --array=0-62`. Follows
+`slurm_patch_only_sweep_agg.sh` conventions exactly (same SBATCH header,
+`exp()` registry, `N_EXP==0` / oversized-array guards, unquoted `--override`
+word-splitting). Writes to `outputs/proto_zscore_results.txt`.
+
+- **Setting 2** — `diagnostic_pta` + `fusion.mode=patch_only`: raw baseline,
+  z-score, z-score with `min_count=20`. Scale-invariant argmax, so no tau sweep;
+  this is the cleanest read on whether z-scoring helps.
+- **Setting 1** — `patch_modulated_pta`: raw baseline, z-score × `tau_patch_proto
+  ∈ {0.5, 1, 2, 5}`, and z-score + `patch_squash=tanh` at the original tau=20.
+
+### `configs/diagnostic_pta/caltech101.yaml`, `ucf101.yaml` — new, 2 lines each
+
+Two-line `defaults:` stubs. `configs/diagnostic_pta/` previously covered only 5
+datasets, so without these the two settings could not sweep the same 7-dataset
+cross-domain core.
+
+---
+
+## Files modified
+
+### `utils/kmeans.py` (+60 / −3)
+
+Extended `_gaussian_score_for_class` (line 117) with `proto_mu`, `proto_sigma`,
+`proto_valid`, `sigma_eps` kwargs.
+
+New aggregation branch inserted after `app_w` is computed, **before** the
+existing raw chain, implementing the doc's formula verbatim:
+
+```python
+z = _zscore(best_per_proto, proto_mu, proto_sigma, proto_valid, sigma_eps)
+w_norm = app_w / app_w.sum().clamp(min=1e-6)      # doc §2.1
+z_weighted = w_norm * z
+score = z_weighted.sum()                          # doc S_c
+```
+
+- `zscore_weighted_mean` — the doc's weighted mean z-score.
+- `zscore_top_m_mean` — top-k of `w_norm * z`, for comparison.
+
+The `return_details` dict gains `mu`, `sigma`, `z`, `w_norm` while `best_per_proto`
+still carries the **raw** score, satisfying doc requirements #11 and #12
+(raw-vs-z comparison).
+
+**Bug fixed along the way:** the early returns at old lines 140-141 and 211-212
+returned a bare tensor even when `return_details=True`, crashing the caller's
+2-tuple unpack. Latent before (details were test-only) but the new path enables
+details in production, so both now honor the flag.
+
+### `models/patch_level/gaussian_patch.py` (+109 / −3)
+
+Four sites:
+
+1. **`init_state`** — adds the three accumulators via `proto_stats.init_stats(0, device)`.
+
+2. **`compute_patch_logits`** — reads the new config keys; enables statistics when
+   `aggregation.startswith("zscore")` or `proto_stats_track` is set. Per class it
+   derives `mu`/`sigma`/`valid` and passes them into scoring. It requests details
+   internally (`want_details = return_details or stats_enabled`) because the
+   z-path needs per-prototype raw scores. **After the entire class loop**, it calls
+   `_accumulate_proto_stats`.
+
+   > That ordering *is* the no-leakage guarantee: all scoring reads statistics
+   > first, all writes happen afterwards. The docstring now flags that this
+   > `compute_*` method mutates `states`.
+
+3. **`_accumulate_proto_stats`** (new method) — folds the image into every class's
+   statistics, refreshes `self.last_stats_diag` (`n_protos`, `n_valid`,
+   `n_low_var`, `mean_sigma`), and emits a rate-limited log line every
+   `proto_stats_log_every` calls.
+
+4. **`update_state`** — index lockstep, the highest-risk part of the change:
+   - `proto_stats.grow(...)` after `updated_apps` is built.
+   - `proto_stats.permute(updated_stats, keep)` inside the `> max_K` prune block,
+     right next to `updated_apps = updated_apps[keep]`. Omitting this would
+     silently attach every prototype's history to a *different* prototype.
+   - `state.update(updated_stats)` on write-back.
+
+### `models/fusion.py` (+27 / −3)
+
+`WeightedFusion.__init__` gains `patch_squash` (`none`|`tanh`, default `none`) and
+`patch_squash_scale` (default `3.0`), plus a `_squash_patch()` helper applied to
+the patch term in all three `forward` methods (`WeightedFusion`,
+`ProtoAlphaFusion`, `QualityGatedFusion`).
+
+Default `none` is a strict no-op. `tanh` is monotonic, so it cannot change a
+patch-only argmax — it only matters for the linear fusion in setting 1.
+
+### `models/patch_modulated_pta.py` (+4 / −1)
+
+- Its `__init__` rebuilds `fusion_cfg` from scratch with an explicit key list, so
+  it would have **silently dropped** the new squash keys. Both are now threaded
+  through.
+- Now honors the `RESULT_FILE` env var instead of hardcoding
+  `outputs/result.txt`, matching `diagnostic_pta.py:175`. Without this the sweep
+  could not collect both settings into one file.
+
+### `tests/debug_gaussian_patch.py` (+82 / −12)
+
+- New args: `--aggregation` (all 6 existing modes plus both `zscore_*`),
+  `--top-m`, `--proto-stats-min-count`. `_build_cfg` no longer hardcodes
+  `"aggregation": "weighted_mean"` or `soft_nn_top_m: 4`.
+- `--proto-stats-min-count` defaults to **2**, not the production 10 — this script
+  only walks ~6 images, so the production default would leave every prototype in
+  warm-up and every z-score at 0.
+- New `_print_proto_table()` prints exactly the doc's "Expected Output for
+  Debugging": per class, per prototype `raw_score | mu | sigma | z_score | app_w
+  | norm_w`, then `final_class_score`, then the predicted class. Falls back to a
+  raw-only layout for non-z aggregations.
+- Crop-strip figure annotations extended from `s=… → w=…` to
+  `s=… μ=… σ=… z=… → w=…` when z-scores are present.
+
+### `configs/base.yaml` (+11)
+
+Five `patch_level` keys (`proto_stats_track`, `proto_stats_min_count`,
+`proto_stats_sigma_eps`, `proto_stats_sigma_warn`, `proto_stats_log_every`) and
+two `fusion` keys (`patch_squash`, `patch_squash_scale`). `aggregation` is
+deliberately left unset so the code default `top_m_mean` keeps existing runs
+unchanged.
+
+### `configs/diagnostic_pta/diagnostic_pta.yaml` (+1 / −1)
+
+`fusion.mode: interpolate` → `patch_only`, and the stale comment
+(`interpolate | alpha_gate | tau_gate | hybrid`) corrected to
+`patch_only | image_only`.
+
+**This was a live crash**, not cosmetic: `models/diagnostic_pta.py:130` rejects
+anything but `patch_only`/`image_only`, so any `diagnostic_pta` run using the
+checked-in config raised `ValueError` on the first batch. Only the SLURM script's
+`--override` was keeping it alive.
+
+---
+
+## Verification
+
+The remote Jetson (10.88.111.59) was unreachable — SSH timed out — so **no GPU or
+real-dataset run was performed**. Verified on CPU instead (torch 2.2.2 is
+available locally; only torchvision is missing, which was stubbed).
+
+**39/39 checks pass:**
+
+- `mu` matches `torch.mean`; `sigma` matches `torch.std(unbiased=True)`.
+- Constant-score prototypes land on the eps floor rather than dividing by zero.
+- `S_c = Σ w'ᵢ·zᵢ` with `Σ w' = 1`, and `z = (raw−mu)/sigma`, across every
+  class-scoring in a synthetic stream.
+- **No leakage:** reference count at image *i* never exceeds *i*.
+- **Prune lockstep:** with `max_K=3` forcing eviction, `score_count/sum/sqsum`
+  stay the same length as `centers`/`appearance`; survivors keep their history;
+  `mu`/`sigma` stay finite with `sigma > 0`.
+- Cold-start prototypes abstain at `z=0`; `proto_stats_track` toggles
+  accumulation independently of the aggregation.
+- Zero-patch input honours `return_details` (the fixed unpack crash).
+- `patch_squash=none` is a no-op; `tanh` applies `tanh(z/scale)` and is monotonic.
+
+**No regression:** traces from all 6 raw aggregations over 14 images (including
+pruning) are **byte-identical** to a pristine `git archive HEAD` copy.
+
+**Doc conformance:** `_print_proto_table` reproduces the doc's worked example
+exactly — Class A = 1.6 `(0.5·3.0 + 0.3·1.0 + 0.2·−1.0)`, Class B = 0.8,
+prediction A.
+
+A real bug was found and fixed during verification: `sorted()` over the details
+dict crashed on the mixed `int` class keys and the `"keep_mask"` string key,
+which would have fired on every `debug_gaussian_patch.py` run with a
+`--filter-modes` other than `none` — the script's documented main use.
+
+### Still outstanding
+
+Requires the remote host:
+
+1. `MAX_BATCHES=50` baseline on `patch_modulated_pta` vs `main` (accuracy parity).
+2. `tests/test_pta_determinism.py` and `tests/test_vs_original.py` — the golden
+   snapshots in `tests/fidelity_snapshots/` that the CPU harness cannot substitute for.
+3. Smoke tests of both settings, and `sbatch scripts/slurm_proto_zscore.sh`.
+
+---
+
+## Known caveat, deliberately not addressed
+
+`quality_gate = proto_var / (proto_var + quality_eps)`
+(`gaussian_patch.py:241`) uses `quality_eps=1e-3`, tuned for scores in `[0,1]`.
+On the z scale the across-class variance is far larger, so the gate saturates to
+~1.0.
+
+Inert for `ProtoAlphaFusion` (the configured default, which ignores the gate),
+but it *also* modulates the image-level EMA in `patch_modulated_pta` via
+`quality_modulation`. Flagged in the SLURM script header as a follow-up sweep
+axis on `patch_level.quality_eps` rather than retuned blind.
